<title>USA: AFTER THE BELL - 3Com rises on earnings.</title>
<headline>AFTER THE BELL - 3Com rises on earnings.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of 3Com Corp rose 2-1/8 to 58-3/4 Thursday after hours on news of a jump in first quarter earnings, traders said.</p>
<p>3Com reported earnings of $0.52 a share for the first quarter ended August 31, compared to $0.33 a share the previous first quarter. Revenues rose 42 percent to $707 million from $497 million.</p>
<p>Traders said that there was not much activity in shares other than 3Com.</p>
<p>The New York Stock Exchange said that Dallas Semiconductor Corp, Checkpoint Systems Inc and Apria Healthcare Group Inc were unavailable for trading for news.</p>
<p>The NYSE said session one volume was 3,000 shares, compared to 8,500 shares Monday. Session two volume was 2,263,100 versus 5,078,261.</p>
<p>The American Stock Exchange said there was no after-hours activity.</p>
